{
  "_comment": "Native forms of science, geography and astronomy terms and of people, per locale, as each country's universities, schools and space agency write them (operator 2026-10-17). Vehicle, mission, agency and company names are NOT here — they follow the origin rule (src/lib/name-origins.js). Unsure forms were checked against native pages; `sources` records where. Order of locales: ru ja zh-CN ko hi ar sr-Cyrl de fr es it nl pt-BR.",
  "sources": {
    "hi:planets": "NCERT class 6 'सौरमंडल से पृथ्वी' via shaalaa.com / iasexamportal.com: बुध, शुक्र, पृथ्वी, मंगल, बृहस्पति, शनि, अरुण, वरुण, यम (प्लूटो); bharatdiscovery.org/india/सौरमण्डल: अरुण (यूरेनस), वरुण (नेपच्यून)",
    "ar:Ryugu,Arrokoth,Bennu": "qna.org.qa (ريوغو), aljazeera.net (أروكوث), youm7.com (ريوجو وبينو)",
    "features": "Wikidata sitelinks = each language Wikipedia title (scripts/i18n-tools/wikidata-labels.mjs → maps/2026-10-17-translation-cleanup/wikidata-features.tsv). ru/ja/zh/ko/ar/sr translate maria and Mars features; de/es/it/nl/pt keep Latin IAU names; fr per frwiki title (Mer de la Tranquillité, but Mare Crisium). zh-CN converted to simplified. hi: no hiwiki articles — meaning translated like ja/zh/ru (शांति सागर); Mars-feature forms without a native article follow the nearest language pattern and are unverified. Every cell whose locale shows \"-\" in wikidata-features.tsv (no article in that language) is a constructed form, unverified: Mars features in ko/hi/ar/sr-Cyrl, Hadley–Apennine and Fra Mauro in most locales, Margaritifer Sinus and Aeolis Mons (no Wikidata hit), Shioli in zh-CN.",
    "places": "Each language Wikipedia title via wikidata-labels.mjs (maps/2026-10-17-translation-cleanup/wikidata-launch-sites.tsv). Launch sites are places: native in every locale where its Wikipedia writes them natively; de/it/nl keep Cape Canaveral. Pad codes (SLC-40, LC-39A) unchanged. Unverified (no article in that language): sr-Cyrl Кејп Канаверал, Ђиуцјуен, Тајјуен, Венчанг, Сичанг, Старбејс, Танегашима; ar/hi Jiuquan..Xichang where \"-\"; Starbase in ja/ko/hi/ar.",
    "station": "ISS: every Wikipedia uses its own language name; abbreviation in text: ru МКС, sr-Cyrl МСС (Међународна свемирска станица), es EEI; zh-CN and ar use the full name; others write ISS.",
    "facility": "Whole facility names = each language Wikipedia title (wikidata-launch-sites.tsv), lower-cased where they run inside a sentence. Unverified where that language has no article (sr-Cyrl, hi for most, Air Force Station forms)."
  },
